# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Next.js project following the official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights@^2.0.0` using npm
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with resolved dependencies

### 2. Code Configuration
**Modified: `src/app/layout.tsx`**
- Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component to the root layout's body section
- Placed alongside the existing `<Analytics />` component for consistency

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows Vercel's official Next.js App Router guidelines:
- Used the `/next` import path for Next.js-specific SpeedInsights component
- Placed the component in the root layout file for application-wide tracking
- Component is placed at the end of the body, following the existing Analytics component pattern

## Verification

- ✅ Linter passed with no errors
- ✅ Package successfully installed
- ✅ Code changes follow existing project patterns
- ✅ TypeScript compilation succeeds (verified via linter)

Note: Full build verification requires Supabase environment variables (pre-existing requirement).

## Next Steps

To complete the Speed Insights setup:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel project dashboard
3. Data collection will begin automatically after deployment

